### Every response, success or error, uses the same envelope:
### { "status", "message", "data", "errors", "errorCode", "timestamp" }
### Success: "data" = payload, "errors" = [], "errorCode" = null
### Error:   "data" = null, "errors" = field problems (or []), "errorCode" = e.g. "RESOURCE_NOT_FOUND"

### ===================== Books =====================

### Search → 200, data = { "content": [...], "page": { "number", "size", "totalElements", "totalPages" } }
### Each book has "author": { "id", "name" } and "genres": [ { "id", "name" } ]
GET http://localhost:8080/api/books?genre=classic&size=2

### One book → 200, data = the book
GET http://localhost:8080/api/books/1

### Unknown book → 404, data = null, errorCode = RESOURCE_NOT_FOUND
GET http://localhost:8080/api/books/999

### Invalid filter → 400, errors = [ { "field": "pageRangeValid", "message": "..." } ]
GET http://localhost:8080/api/books?minPages=500&maxPages=100

### ===================== Shelf =====================

### Add Dune to Sara's shelf as READING → 201, data.startedAt = today, data.book = { "id", "title", "pages", "author" }
POST http://localhost:8080/api/shelf
Content-Type: application/json

{ "userId": 1, "bookId": 1, "status": "READING" }

### Add a FINISHED book → 201, data.currentPage = last page, data.finishedAt = today
POST http://localhost:8080/api/shelf
Content-Type: application/json

{ "userId": 1, "bookId": 3, "status": "FINISHED" }

### No status → defaults to WANT_TO_READ
POST http://localhost:8080/api/shelf
Content-Type: application/json

{ "userId": 1, "bookId": 2 }

### Same book again → 409, errorCode = DUPLICATE_RESOURCE
POST http://localhost:8080/api/shelf
Content-Type: application/json

{ "userId": 1, "bookId": 1, "status": "READING" }

### Sara's shelf → 200, first page (20 per page, oldest entry first)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/shelf?userId=1

### Sara's shelf, 2 per page, second page, sorted by book title
GET http://localhost:8080/api/shelf?userId=1&page=1&size=2&sort=book.title

### ===================== Stats =====================

### Sara's reading stats for 2026 → 200, data = { "userId", "year", "booksFinished", "pagesRead", "finishedByGenre" }
GET http://localhost:8080/api/users/1/stats?year=2026

### ===================== Activity =====================

### Latest events, newest first → 200, data = { "events": [ { "timestamp": "...Z", "message": "..." } ] }
GET http://localhost:8080/api/activity
